# estimator — the CLI's source is committed, its data never is (design R3 §4, §10 Q11)
estimator/estimator.db*
estimator/spool/
estimator/backups/
estimator/sweep.lock
# P2.7: the rendered board carries real subjects, real ids and real figures — local
# only, same rule as the DB itself. `--out <dir>` can point elsewhere, but the
# default location (alongside estimator.db) must never be committable.
estimator/board.html
estimator/board.md
# gate probes: the .ts scanners are code and committed; everything they PRODUCE is
# corpus-derived data and stays local — this repo is public (decision 11: no
# estimate/actual/spend data, no prompt or conversation content, ever)
estimator/gates/*.json
estimator/gates/*.md
# the spec and decision log quote private prompts and real usage data — local only,
# covered by the weekly backups/ snapshot, not by git
estimator/DESIGN.md
estimator/DECISIONS.md
# `bun install` materialises the two typecheck-only devDependencies here. Runtime
# dependencies are still zero; `bun.lock` IS committed, so `bun run typecheck`
# reproduces exactly the compiler the last recorded run used.
estimator/node_modules/
daemon-auth-cooldown
daemon-auth-status.json
